<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8"/>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"/>
    <base href="/"/>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Roboto:300,400,500,700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet"/>
    <link href=@Assets["_content/MudBlazor/MudBlazor.min.css"] rel="stylesheet"/>
    <ImportMap/>
@*
    Prerendering is deliberately off, here and on Routes below.

    The JWT lives in the browser's localStorage, which the server cannot read. Every render
    resolves the authentication state — MainLayout wraps the whole application in an
    <AuthorizeView>, so even /login goes through it — and that resolution ends in a JS interop
    call. During a prerender pass there is no browser, so the call throws. No page of this
    application is prerenderable; this is the root of the component tree, not a page-level
    detail to work around.

    Even if it were made to work, the gain would be negative. The public pages are built on
    interactive MudBlazor controls, which a prerendered pass renders inert: a login form the
    user can see and type into but that silently drops the click until WebAssembly boots.
    The pages that load data do so in OnInitializedAsync, which prerendering runs twice — the
    server pass having no token, it would spend a 401 round-trip per page.

    Serving this application over SSR would mean moving the token into a cookie behind a
    backend-for-frontend, so the server knows the caller at render time. That is a sound
    pattern, but it buys nothing here: the application is entirely behind authentication, so
    there is no SEO to gain, and it would put a second authentication model next to the bearer
    JWT the API and its integration tests are built on.
*@
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="new InteractiveWebAssemblyRenderMode(prerender: false)"/>
</head>

<body>
<Routes @rendermode="new InteractiveWebAssemblyRenderMode(prerender: false)"/>
<script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
<script src=@Assets["_content/MudBlazor/MudBlazor.min.js"]></script>
</body>

</html>
